  "requirement": "The Habeas Codicem project MUST keep its mdBook Markdown in `md/` and Rust source in `src/`, and its own book MUST use the Habeas preprocessor.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. The subject has three obligations, and each has code and a test.\n\n**1. Keep the mdBook Markdown in `md/`.**\n- `book.toml` `[book] src = \"md\"` (marked {impl}) sets the book's source directory.\n- `tests/repository.rs::project_book_uses_the_repository_local_preprocessor_alias` (marked {test}) asserts `book.src == \"md\"` and that `md/SUMMARY.md` exists.\n\n**2. Keep the Rust source in `src/`.**\n- `Cargo.toml` `[lib] path = \"src/lib.rs\"` and `[[bin]] path = \"src/main.rs\"` (both marked {impl}) point the crate targets into `src/`.\n- `crate_targets_are_declared_in_src` asserts the lib path, that there is exactly one bin named `habeas`, and that the bin path is `src/main.rs`.\n- The alias test also asserts that `src/lib.rs` and `src/main.rs` exist.\n\n**3. The project's own book uses the Habeas preprocessor.**\n- `book.toml` `[preprocessor.habeas] command = \"cargo habeas mdbook\"` (marked {impl}) configures the preprocessor.\n- The alias test asserts that command and the `html` renderer. It also asserts that the `.cargo/config.toml` alias `habeas = \"run --release -p habeas --\"` exists, so the command resolves to the repository-local binary.\n\nThe `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml` entries set no behavior beyond what the requirement states.",
